# Key Takeaways

* Always perform a full TCP port scan.
* Enumerate every exposed web service independently.
* Review page source when investigating web applications.
* Identify the encoding or data format before attempting to decode it.
* Identify the hash type before attempting to crack it.
* Images may contain hidden information.
* Enumerate scheduled tasks after obtaining shell access.
* Writable scripts executed with elevated privileges can lead to full system compromise.

